{
  "_about": [
    "Golden cases for which self-notes a device acts on: whose signature counts, which notes act, and that a note acts once.",
    "Normative: docs/sealed-messages.md §Signed notes.",
    "The sealing and signing of a note are pinned in mls/fixtures/account-store.json (note_sender, note_open_signed); this table pins the decisions around them.",
    "`seenKeepMs` is how long a note id acted on is remembered.",
    "`senders`: `self` is the receiving device, `devices` its account's device list, `sender` the note's claimed sender. A device row is {id, revoked, accountCertified, approvalState, signingKeyHex}; an omitted field reads as revoked false, accountCertified true, approvalState \"approved\" and signingKeyHex 32 bytes of 0xaa. `expect` is the signing key the note is opened under (hex), or null: the note is dropped.",
    "`verdicts`: whether a note that opened acts. `note` is {kind, sender, asker}: `sender` \"\" is an unsigned note, which never acts, and `asker` is a `history` note's `d`. `state` is {handoffWanted}.",
    "`seen`: `ledger` maps a note id acted on (hex) to when it is forgotten (epoch milliseconds); `expect` is true when the note with `noteIdHex` at `nowMs` was already acted on and must not act again.",
    "`answers`: what a device sends a sibling it hands history to (one that asked, by a signed or unsigned note, or one it owes a hand-off), by the `OwnDeviceVerdict` name that `check_own_device_key` gives for that sibling's row (its id, signing key, `approved_by_device_id` and `approval_signature`): `history` is the hand-off, `none` the nothing-to-send note. A verdict the reader does not know is `none`. The hand-off a device sends as it approves another skips this check: it has just signed that approval.",
    "To replay: run each case through your own implementation of the format and compare the result with the case's expectation, field by field."
  ],
